# Model weights and checkpoints
# Kaggle serves notebook outputs as .zip, and torch.save itself writes a zip
# container -- so a downloaded checkpoint often arrives named *.zip and would NOT
# be caught by the *.pth rule below. These run 13-110 MB each; a full 12-arm run
# is close to a gigabyte.
results/checkpoints/*.zip
**/results/checkpoints/*.zip
*.crdownload
# A torch checkpoint IS a zip container, so double-clicking one gets it unpacked by
# macOS Archive Utility into a directory of raw tensor shards (data/0, data/1, ...).
# One 110 MB checkpoint becomes ~240 untracked files; nine of them, 2175 files and
# 710 MB. Re-zip the directory to recover a loadable .pth -- see progress.md.
**/results/checkpoints/*/
*.pth
*.pt
*.pth.tar
*.tar
*.ckpt
*.pb
*.h5
*.pkl
*.pickle

